{
  "dom_id": "step-456178",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Sine",
  "problem": "Given the triangle below, find the length of $\\overline{NO}$ rounded to one decimal place.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14203245/assets/9108818debc297388dde73a7aa7689eac263c6ec033643c7e2bcdfb3677a8f44.png)",
  "worked_solution": "For an angle $\\theta$ in a right triangle, the trigonometric ratios are as follows:\n\n- $\\sin\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}}$\n\n- $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\textrm{opposite leg}}{\\textrm{adjacent leg}}$\n\nFirst, notice that we are given the length of the leg $\\overline{MO}$ opposite the given angle $\\angle{N}$ and wish to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overline{NO}.$\n\nThe trigonometric ratio that relates the opposite leg to the hypotenuse is *sine*. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(m∠N) & =\\frac{\\text{opposite leg}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘}) & =\\frac{20}{NO} \\\\ NO\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘}) & =20 \\\\ NO & =\\frac{20}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing a calculator to evaluate the trigonometric ratio, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}NO & =\\frac{20}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({32}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{(0.529\\,91…)} \\\\  & =37.741\\,59… \\\\  & ≈37.7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-456178\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"456178\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"3249\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-456178\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-2\">Calculating an Unknown Side Length Using Sine</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"456178\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                  